1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,038
Hi, and welcome to PadDeck!

2
00:00:02,038 --> 00:00:07,703
In this short series, I'll show you how to turn an Android tablet or phone into a

3
00:00:07,703 --> 00:00:10,570
wireless Stream Deck for your Windows PC.

4
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:13,739
A Stream Deck is a panel of buttons.

5
00:00:13,739 --> 00:00:17,991
Each button does something on your computer with a single tap,

6
00:00:17,991 --> 00:00:22,380
like muting your microphone, opening an app, or playing a sound.

7
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:29,011
With PadDeck, your tablet shows the buttons, and your PC carries out the actions.

8
00:00:29,011 --> 00:00:32,159
Watch: tapping Task Manager, YouTube Music,

9
00:00:32,159 --> 00:00:36,040
and Discord opens them on the computer straight away.

10
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:41,111
On the computer, PadDeck Desktop runs quietly in the background.

11
00:00:41,111 --> 00:00:45,960
It also includes the Stream Deck Editor, where you design every button.

12
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:51,377
You'll need a Windows 10 or 11 PC, an Android tablet or phone,

13
00:00:51,377 --> 00:00:54,877
and one Wi-Fi network that both devices share.

14
00:00:54,877 --> 00:00:57,920
There's no account, and no subscription.

15
00:00:58,681 --> 00:01:03,841
In this video, we'll install PadDeck on your PC and on your tablet.

16
00:01:04,541 --> 00:01:08,510
First, open the PadDeck Releases page on GitHub,

17
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:13,389
and download two files: the PadDeck setup file for Windows,

18
00:01:13,389 --> 00:01:16,201
and PadDeck dot A P K for Android.

19
00:01:16,901 --> 00:01:19,824
On your PC, double-click the setup file.

20
00:01:19,824 --> 00:01:25,524
If Windows shows a blue box saying Windows protected your PC, click More info,

21
00:01:25,524 --> 00:01:26,693
then Run anyway.

22
00:01:26,693 --> 00:01:30,786
It appears because the installer isn't digitally signed.

23
00:01:30,786 --> 00:01:33,051
Then click Install, and Finish.

24
00:01:33,751 --> 00:01:38,563
PadDeck opens, and a blue PadDeck icon appears in the system tray,

25
00:01:38,563 --> 00:01:41,187
at the bottom right of your taskbar.

26
00:01:41,187 --> 00:01:45,561
If Windows Firewall asks, allow PadDeck on private networks.

27
00:01:46,261 --> 00:01:49,026
Now let's install the app on your tablet.

28
00:01:49,026 --> 00:01:52,533
In PadDeck on your PC, click Devices in the sidebar,

29
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:55,501
and find the box called Get the Android app.

30
00:01:56,201 --> 00:02:01,117
Scan that code with your tablet's camera, and open the downloaded file.

31
00:02:01,117 --> 00:02:07,071
When Android asks, allow installing apps from this source, then tap Install, and Open.

32
00:02:07,825 --> 00:02:12,395
This is the most important step: connecting your tablet to your PC.

33
00:02:12,395 --> 00:02:14,305
You only need to do it once.

34
00:02:15,005 --> 00:02:20,696
Before connecting, make sure your PC and your tablet are on the same Wi-Fi network,

35
00:02:20,696 --> 00:02:23,302
and that PadDeck is running on the PC.

36
00:02:23,302 --> 00:02:27,415
Guest networks usually block devices from seeing each other.

37
00:02:28,115 --> 00:02:32,454
On your PC, open PadDeck and click Devices in the sidebar.

38
00:02:32,454 --> 00:02:37,091
Here you'll find a large QR code and a six digit pairing code.

39
00:02:37,091 --> 00:02:41,055
Each code works once, and expires after five minutes.

40
00:02:41,755 --> 00:02:43,847
On the tablet, open PadDeck.

41
00:02:43,847 --> 00:02:46,836
You'll see the Pair with your PC screen.

42
00:02:46,836 --> 00:02:52,215
Tap Scan QR code, and point the camera at the QR code on your PC screen.

43
00:02:52,915 --> 00:02:56,983
Or, tap your PC in the list of PCs found on this network,

44
00:02:56,983 --> 00:02:59,696
and type the six digits on the keypad.

45
00:02:59,696 --> 00:03:03,335
Pairing starts as soon as you enter the last digit.

46
00:03:04,035 --> 00:03:06,960
When pairing succeeds, your buttons appear.

47
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:12,470
Look at the top: a green dot, and the word Connected, mean everything is working.

48
00:03:12,470 --> 00:03:17,095
The number shows how many milliseconds a tap takes to reach your PC.

49
00:03:17,795 --> 00:03:22,924
On the PC, your tablet now appears under Paired devices, with a green dot.

50
00:03:22,924 --> 00:03:25,765
You can remove a device here at any time.

51
00:03:26,465 --> 00:03:30,899
If it doesn't connect, check both devices use the same Wi-Fi,

52
00:03:30,899 --> 00:03:36,931
make sure PadDeck is running, and click Allow through firewall on the Devices page.

53
00:03:36,931 --> 00:03:39,548
If the code expired, press New code.

54
00:03:39,548 --> 00:03:44,344
An amber dot means connecting or slow, and red means disconnected.

55
00:03:44,344 --> 00:03:46,815
PadDeck keeps retrying on its own.

56
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:52,060
Let's take a tour of the PadDeck screen, so you know what every part does.

57
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:59,226
On the left are the sections: Stream Deck, Soundboard, Control Centre, Audio, Apps,

58
00:03:59,226 --> 00:04:01,330
and Settings at the bottom.

59
00:04:02,030 --> 00:04:07,541
Across the top are your pages: Home, Work, Gaming, and Creative.

60
00:04:07,541 --> 00:04:09,780
Tap a page name to switch.

61
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:13,967
Next to the connection badge is the current profile.

62
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:17,990
Tap it to switch to another profile, such as Work or Gaming.

63
00:04:18,690 --> 00:04:24,430
The Edit button, at the top right, lets you add, move, and change tiles.

64
00:04:25,130 --> 00:04:30,016
At the bottom you have a volume slider, the current speakers or headphones,

65
00:04:30,016 --> 00:04:31,709
and the microphone button.

66
00:04:31,709 --> 00:04:37,507
The green Live button at the top is your microphone too: green means people can hear you,

67
00:04:37,507 --> 00:04:38,550
red means muted.

68
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:46,526
On the PC, the sidebar lists Dashboard, Stream Deck Editor, Applications, Soundboard,

69
00:04:46,526 --> 00:04:50,550
Audio Control, Profiles, Devices, and Settings.

70
00:04:51,321 --> 00:04:57,871
Now let's make PadDeck yours: adding apps, rearranging tiles, and designing buttons.

71
00:04:58,571 --> 00:05:02,788
To add an application, open the Stream Deck Editor on your PC.

72
00:05:02,788 --> 00:05:07,141
In the Add to deck panel, type the app's name in the search box.

73
00:05:07,841 --> 00:05:09,570
Click Add next to the app.

74
00:05:09,570 --> 00:05:13,361
PadDeck creates a tile with the app's real icon and name,

75
00:05:13,361 --> 00:05:16,288
and it appears on your tablet straight away.

76
00:05:16,288 --> 00:05:19,481
You can also drag the app onto any empty square.

77
00:05:20,181 --> 00:05:24,549
The Applications page lists everything PadDeck found on your PC.

78
00:05:24,549 --> 00:05:27,894
Choose a page in the Add to menu, then click Add.

79
00:05:27,894 --> 00:05:30,761
Press Rescan if you install something new.

80
00:05:31,461 --> 00:05:33,360
To change a tile, click it.

81
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:37,581
The Button designer opens on the right, with a live preview.

82
00:05:38,281 --> 00:05:44,230
Use the Action tab to choose what it does, the Design tab to change its icon, colours,

83
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:48,311
and size, and the Toggle tab to give it an on and off look.

84
00:05:49,011 --> 00:05:52,271
To rearrange, drag a tile onto another square.

85
00:05:52,271 --> 00:05:57,233
Drop it on another tile to swap them, on a page name to move it there,

86
00:05:57,233 --> 00:05:59,501
or on a folder to put it inside.

87
00:06:00,201 --> 00:06:02,663
You can do the same on the tablet.

88
00:06:02,663 --> 00:06:07,951
Tap Edit, drag tiles around, or tap an empty square to add something new.

89
00:06:08,651 --> 00:06:16,193
Long-press any tile for quick options: edit, duplicate, move to another page, or delete.

90
00:06:16,193 --> 00:06:17,478
Made a mistake?

91
00:06:17,478 --> 00:06:18,421
Press Undo.

92
00:06:19,215 --> 00:06:22,315
Here's what every button on the Home page does.

93
00:06:23,015 --> 00:06:26,988
Microphone mutes or unmutes your microphone in every app.

94
00:06:26,988 --> 00:06:32,425
The tile turns red and says Mic muted, and turns green again when you're live.

95
00:06:33,125 --> 00:06:37,501
Volume minus and Volume plus change the volume by five percent,

96
00:06:37,501 --> 00:06:39,724
and Mute silences your speakers.

97
00:06:39,724 --> 00:06:42,225
Watch the slider at the bottom move.

98
00:06:42,925 --> 00:06:49,745
Play Pause, Previous, and Next control whatever is playing, like YouTube Music or Spotify.

99
00:06:50,445 --> 00:06:55,154
Screenshot saves a picture of all your screens to Pictures, Screenshots,

100
00:06:55,154 --> 00:06:57,182
and copies it to the clipboard.

101
00:06:57,182 --> 00:07:01,825
Snip opens the Windows snipping tool, so you can capture just one area.

102
00:07:02,525 --> 00:07:07,611
App tiles, like YouTube Music, Discord, and Chrome, open those apps.

103
00:07:07,611 --> 00:07:11,425
A short message at the bottom confirms each action.

104
00:07:12,125 --> 00:07:17,025
Task Manager, Explorer, and Settings open those Windows tools.

105
00:07:17,725 --> 00:07:23,237
Focus lowers the volume, turns off notifications, and mutes the soundboard,

106
00:07:23,237 --> 00:07:24,927
so you can concentrate.

107
00:07:24,927 --> 00:07:27,205
Lock locks Windows immediately.

108
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:32,665
Important: Sleep, Restart, and Shut down affect your whole computer,

109
00:07:32,665 --> 00:07:34,345
so save your work first.

110
00:07:34,345 --> 00:07:37,215
PadDeck always asks you to confirm these,

111
00:07:37,215 --> 00:07:41,415
and Restart and Shut down wait five seconds before starting.

112
00:07:42,183 --> 00:07:44,583
Let's play some sounds with the soundboard.

113
00:07:45,283 --> 00:07:47,821
Open the Soundboard from the left side.

114
00:07:47,821 --> 00:07:52,313
Sounds play through your PC's speakers or headphones, not the tablet.

115
00:07:53,013 --> 00:07:59,136
Use the categories across the top, like Funny Sounds, Memes, or Notifications,

116
00:07:59,136 --> 00:08:00,863
to filter your sounds.

117
00:08:01,563 --> 00:08:03,147
Tap a sound to play it.

118
00:08:03,147 --> 00:08:06,935
Tap again to layer it, and play several sounds at once.

119
00:08:06,935 --> 00:08:10,103
A playing sound shows stop and replay buttons.

120
00:08:10,803 --> 00:08:13,354
Stop all silences everything instantly,

121
00:08:13,354 --> 00:08:17,213
and the slider next to it sets the soundboard's own volume.

122
00:08:17,913 --> 00:08:24,501
To add your own sounds, click Add sounds, and choose MP3, WAV, or OGG files.

123
00:08:24,501 --> 00:08:31,523
Long-press a sound to rename it, or change its icon, colour, category, or volume.

124
00:08:32,310 --> 00:08:36,030
The Control Centre shows your PC's health at a glance.

125
00:08:36,730 --> 00:08:40,458
Here you'll see CPU, graphics, and memory usage,

126
00:08:40,458 --> 00:08:44,030
with temperatures where Windows provides them.

127
00:08:44,730 --> 00:08:50,015
The YouTube Music card shows the current song, artwork, and progress.

128
00:08:50,015 --> 00:08:53,920
You can play, pause, skip, or drag the bar to seek.

129
00:08:54,620 --> 00:09:00,309
You'll also see mouse and keyboard battery for Bluetooth devices, plus storage,

130
00:09:00,309 --> 00:09:02,182
network speed, and uptime.

131
00:09:02,182 --> 00:09:07,510
If a value isn't available, PadDeck says Unavailable, instead of guessing.

132
00:09:08,210 --> 00:09:12,574
The Audio section switches speakers and microphones with one tap,

133
00:09:12,574 --> 00:09:15,460
and sets the volume of each app separately.

134
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:19,702
On the PC, the same information is on the Dashboard.

135
00:09:19,702 --> 00:09:24,060
Press Customize to choose which cards appear, and in what order.

136
00:09:24,832 --> 00:09:26,283
Something not working?

137
00:09:26,283 --> 00:09:29,582
Here are quick fixes for the most common problems.

138
00:09:30,282 --> 00:09:34,744
If your tablet can't connect, put both devices on the same Wi-Fi,

139
00:09:34,744 --> 00:09:37,696
check the PadDeck icon is in the PC's tray,

140
00:09:37,696 --> 00:09:41,061
click Allow through firewall on the Devices page,

141
00:09:41,061 --> 00:09:44,082
or type the address shown under the QR code.

142
00:09:44,782 --> 00:09:48,406
If a button does nothing, check the badge says Connected,

143
00:09:48,406 --> 00:09:51,522
and read the message at the bottom of the screen.

144
00:09:51,522 --> 00:09:53,684
Make sure you're not in Edit mode.

145
00:09:53,684 --> 00:09:58,962
Note that apps running as administrator ignore keyboard shortcuts from normal apps.

146
00:09:59,662 --> 00:10:01,467
No sound from the soundboard?

147
00:10:01,467 --> 00:10:06,260
Check the output shown at the top of the soundboard, and turn off Focus mode.

148
00:10:06,260 --> 00:10:11,302
If the mic button doesn't mute, choose the right microphone in the Audio section.

149
00:10:12,002 --> 00:10:16,933
If a tile says Unavailable, the app or file was moved or removed.

150
00:10:16,933 --> 00:10:22,852
Press Rescan on the Applications page, then edit the tile and choose it again.

151
00:10:23,609 --> 00:10:27,739
To finish, here are a few tips to get the most out of PadDeck.

152
00:10:28,439 --> 00:10:33,395
PadDeck adapts when you rotate your tablet, and it works on phones too,

153
00:10:33,395 --> 00:10:35,209
in portrait and landscape.

154
00:10:35,909 --> 00:10:39,651
Make it yours with themes like Dark, AMOLED, or Midnight,

155
00:10:39,651 --> 00:10:43,589
or pick your own colours with a colour picker or a hex code.

156
00:10:44,289 --> 00:10:48,674
Create profiles for different activities, like Work and Gaming,

157
00:10:48,674 --> 00:10:51,249
and switch between them with one tap.

158
00:10:51,949 --> 00:10:54,736
Browse every installed app in the Apps section,

159
00:10:54,736 --> 00:10:57,759
and put the buttons you use most on your Home page.

160
00:10:58,459 --> 00:10:59,813
Thanks for watching!

161
00:10:59,813 --> 00:11:03,806
You'll find the full user guide on the PadDeck GitHub page.

162
00:11:03,806 --> 00:11:04,889
Happy streaming!

